invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: signature_verifies returns without wiping the power it compared.
  That power is the encoded message when the check passes, and a value
  that with the message factors the modulus when it fails.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test copies the stack below one signature and finds
  the encoded message's bytes there.

--- old
    int same = ct_memeq(power, em, k->n_len) != 0;
    ct_wipe(power, sizeof power);
--- new
    int same = ct_memeq(power, em, k->n_len) != 0;
